// This used to be the Microsoft script tag itself, which meant the widget
// loaded on sight and wrote to the visitor's device before anyone was asked.
// It is now only a marker. /assets/js/consent.js finds the marker and injects
// the real widget, but only after the visitor allows chat. The widget's
// organisation and application ids live in consent.js, in one place.
//
// Do not paste the Microsoft snippet back in. A test fails if anyone does.
---

<div data-x4-livechat hidden></div>
